{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{% set output_format_description = "a brief, objective observation (2-3 sentences) focused solely on the primary trend or key comparison shown in the 'New vs. Updated CVEs Monthly' chart data. No interpretation or recommendations." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
The chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Monthly New vs. Updated CVEs') }}' displays the monthly counts of 'New' versus 'Updated' CVEs.
Examine the provided data summary.
Identify and describe the most salient trend or comparison. For instance:
- Was there a consistent dominance of 'New' or 'Updated' CVEs?
- Did any month show a significant spike or deviation in this balance?
- What was the general pattern over the quarter?
Focus only on what the data directly indicates.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('new_vs_updated_monthly') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption }}

Data Summary:
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
Note: If percentages do not sum to 100%, this may be due to some CVEs lacking an assigned value (i.e., missing or NaN values were excluded from the calculation).
{% endblock data_context %}
